{%- comment -%}
  Call the app's resource provider (config.resources_partial, default 'mcp/resources';
  Layer 2, spec §13.1 resources) for ONE operation on behalf of an AUTHENTICATED caller.
  Callers never invoke it for an anonymous request.

  The provider partial receives `operation`, `uri`, `cursor`, `principal` and `agent`
  (the same principal and agent tool handlers get) and returns:
    list      → { resources: [{ uri, name, title?, description?, mimeType?, size? }],
                  next_cursor? }
    templates → { resource_templates: [{ uriTemplate, name, title?, description?, mimeType? }] }
    read      → { contents: [{ uri, mimeType?, text | blob }] }, or nil when the resource
                does not exist OR this caller may not read it (the two must look the
                same, so an existence check leaks nothing)
  The provider applies the app's access rules for the caller: the engine cannot know
  them. The `mcp+page:` scheme is reserved for the engine's markdown pages.

  An app without the partial has no provider (available: false). A provider that
  raises is logged and reported as failed; nothing of the error reaches the caller. A
  partial the provider itself fails to find counts as a failure, not as "no provider":
  only the error naming the provider partial means it is absent.

  @param {string} operation - 'list' | 'templates' | 'read'
  @param {string} uri       - the requested URI (read only)
  @param {string} cursor    - the opaque cursor a previous list returned (list only)
  @param {object} principal - the authenticated principal
  @param {object} agent     - the calling agent
  @return {object} { available:boolean, failed:boolean, value }
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  function cfg = 'modules/mcp/helpers/config'
  assign partial = cfg.resources_partial | default: 'mcp/resources'

  assign out = {
    "available": true,
    "failed": false
  }
  assign value = null
  assign absent_message = 'find partial "' | append: partial | append: '"'
  try
    function value = partial, operation: operation, uri: uri, cursor: cursor, principal: principal, agent: agent
  catch e
    if e.message contains absent_message
      assign out['available'] = false
    else
      assign out['failed'] = true
      assign log_message = operation | append: ': ' | append: e.message
      log log_message, type: 'mcp.resources_provider_error'
    endif
  endtry
  assign out['value'] = value
  return out
%}
